{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2973","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2973","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2973\",\"parent_revision\":\"ed69f482c068bc925f766d42760eccd5648c3edb\",\"root_revision\":\"b775dd0361f5d907d2d52372cdde78302143a1d27c20e16d314b54425c2f9a0c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered while extending rendering.SECTION_HEADING for #2956/PR #2964, directly evidenced by the same corrupted cache data used as ground truth for #2956: #2955's own description text uses \\\"## Entry format\\\" / \\\"## What triggers an entry\\\" / \\\"## End of session\\\" as documentation-style prose headings. On a GitHub round trip these get treated as new top-level sections instead of remaining part of the description, exactly like the entry-block (\\\"## Claim N\\\") fragmentation #2956 fixed -- but Description content is NOT wrapped in the <div><sub>...</sub>...</div> entry convention that protects every other section's content, so #2956's fix (the marko _EntryDivBlock opacity element) does not cover it.\\n\\nConcrete reproduction (render_issue_body -> parse_issue_body on a BacklogItem whose description contains \\\"## Entry format\\\\n\\\\n...\\\\n\\\\n## What triggers an entry\\\\n\\\\n...\\\\n\\\\n## End of session\\\\n\\\\n...\\\"): remote.description ends up as only the text before the FIRST embedded heading (\\\"Run a continuous register.\\\"), and remote.sections gains 3 spurious unknown__ keys for the rest -- the description's own content is silently truncated/redistributed, a real data-loss bug, not a display-quality issue.\\n\\nRoot cause: render_issue_body embeds item.description as bare, unwrapped text (\\\"## Description\\\\n\\\\n{item.description}\\\"), unlike every other section whose entries are rendered through the entry-div wrapper. The top-level \\\"## \\\" section-boundary scan (extract_sections, fixed for entry content in #2956) has no way to distinguish a genuine next top-level section from a heading the user's own description prose happens to contain, because both are syntactically identical flat \\\"## \\\" lines with nothing else to disambiguate them.\\n\\nWhy not fixed inline in #2964: the only clean fix consistent with #2956's existing entry-div convention is wrapping item.description in the same <div><sub>...</sub>...</div> marker when rendering -- but that changes the rendered format of every backlog item's description on GitHub (a <div> wrapper around a top-of-issue description is visually unusual) and requires the parse side to handle BOTH the new wrapped format AND every existing real GitHub issue's current plain/unwrapped \\\"## Description\\\" body for backward compatibility across this repo's ~2900+ real issues. That is a design decision with real blast radius across the live issue history, not a cheap one-line fix, so it needs its own scoped plan rather than expanding #2964 further.\\n\\n**Research first**: confirm the actual scope of affected live issues (how many currently have a description containing its own \\\"## \\\" heading) before committing to a migration approach. Consider whether wrap-on-write with dual-format-read-support is sufficient, or whether a less format-disruptive escaping scheme (e.g. demoting embedded \\\"##\\\" to \\\"###\\\" on render, restoring on parse) is preferable to avoid changing every issue's visual layout.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **description field content containing its own '## ' headings silently loses everything after the first embedded heading on a github round trip** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, found while extending SECTION_HEADING for #2956/#2964\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e0c6b197d6aad4498477c964a59486526bd226fcee6b8ae866ed853e7de3d1cf\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgxdQw\"}"}